+## Secret scanning
+
+The repository tree is scanned for secret-shaped content at two points:
+
+- **CI**: every pull request runs a pinned `gitleaks` tree scan
+  (`.github/workflows/ci-foundation.yml`, `scripts/repo-secret-scan.sh`), in
+  addition to the build-output gate (`scripts/bundle-secret-gate.mjs`).
+- **Pre-commit (local)**: `.githooks/pre-commit` runs `gitleaks protect
+  --staged` over the staged index and blocks the commit on a finding. Enable
+  it once per clone:
+
+  ```sh
+  git config core.hooksPath .githooks
+  ```
+
+  The hook redacts any match and is a no-op when `gitleaks` is not installed
+  (CI remains the authoritative gate).
+
+Historical logs and snapshots under `evidence/` are intentionally public
+fixtures; secret-shaped strings there are audited test data, not credentials.
+Never commit a real credential - host-only secrets live in
+`/home/user/.env` and are never tracked.
+
